SLOOP 2.8.4 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/isod89/sloop-fm1 tag v2.8.4
(commit 91f30182d9095e0ecdb43396554f2ce5a67df179; source: https://github.com/isod89/sloop-fm1/archive/91f30182d9095e0ecdb43396554f2ce5a67df179.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. SLOOP by isod89, based on Felucca: Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments (Felucca); SLOOP's changes and additions by its authors (SLOOP's README, Credits).
Ported parts keep their licences (msfa in fm6_core.c: Apache-2.0; DaisySP and Rings in phys_dsp.c, phys_symp.c: MIT; the Terminus screen font is rasterised in: OFL 1.1), the instrument and drum samples are CC0
(Versilian Studios, Sonic Pi): SLOOP's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file. The icon atlas is a Felucca Asset (Hügelton Instruments), combined under the additional permission
(GPL-3.0 section 7) of LICENSING.md. The JieLi SDK files of SLOOP's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/sloop_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as SLOOP's own host tests do (tests/hostsim.c, editor_host.c, boot_sound_test.c)
and replaces only the hardware: keys/LEDs/LCD, ADC (MASTER; battery full), NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, USB = always configured (SysEx and MIDI out through usb.c's rings),
one core (MENU > 2ND CORE has no second core here), no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no serial console, no USB rescue, no updater (ota.c answers the identity handshake only).
Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h).

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/isod89/sloop-fm1 at commit 91f30182d9095e0ecdb43396554f2ce5a67df179
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py, the glue tools/studio/sloop_studio.c and the shim tools/wasm_shim. A tarball of exactly this commit
(sloop-fm1-91f30182d9095e0ecdb43396554f2ce5a67df179.tar.gz, made with tools/make_source_tarballs.py) is attached to every
FM-1 Companion release that ships this build: https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/releases
Written offer: for at least three years after the last release that ships this build, the maintainers of
FM-1 Companion will give anyone a copy of that corresponding source on request (https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/issues),
free of charge apart from the cost of physically performing the distribution.
